Full-process practical operation of drone aerial image detection case based on PP-YOLOE-SOD
1. Background
The PaddleDetection team provides a PP-YOLOE-based detection model for small target scene datasets such as VisDrone-DET, DOTA horizontal box, and Xview.

2. Solution Introduction
2.1 Data Introduction
VisDrone-DET is a dataset of small objects captured by drones in aerial photography. Download the organized VisDrone-DET dataset in COCO format and the sliced ​​dataset in COCO format . It detects 10 categories , including pedestrian(1), people(2), bicycle(3), car(4), van(5), truck(6), tricycle(7), awning-tricycle(8), bus(9), motor(10)the original dataset .

2.2 Model selection
2.2.1 Basic Model
We use PP-YOLOE+ for training. PP-YOLOE is a high-precision and fast inference detection model that includes the backbone network CSPRepResNet, feature fusion CSPPAN, lightweight ETHead, and an improved dynamic matching algorithm TAL. We also designed a series of models based on different application scenarios, namely s/m/l/x.
Easy to deploy. PP-YOLOE can export onnx, use paddle inference, tensorrt and other deployment methods, and provide rich deployment demos, ready to use out of the box.
2.2.2 Optimization plan
Solution 1: Use the SAHI (Slicing Aided Hyper Inference) tool to slice and jigsaw puzzles. Users can download the model for use.
Solution 2: Single model optimization, introducing the Transformer global attention mechanism; in the Anchor-free framework, introducing a dynamic matching mechanism with a center prior, and proposing a vector-based DFL regression algorithm
