3.2.3 SAHI Cutting
SAHI (Slicing Aided Hyper Inference) is a lightweight vision library for performing large-scale image detection and instance segmentation. It is primarily used for assisted inference scenarios, without requiring a complete redesign of the model architecture. PaddleDetection integrates image slicing and tiling functionality, allowing for direct use within the detection framework. It also provides tools for both training and inference scenarios.

ACTUALLY

