Notice:

--slice_infer means slice prediction and assemble the reconstructed results. If not used, leave it blank.
--slice_size indicates the size of the sliced ​​sub-image, and --overlap_ratio indicates the overlap ratio between sub-images.
--combine_method indicates the method of recombining and deduplicating subgraph results, the default is nms;
--match_threshold indicates the threshold for deduplication of subgraph results, the default value is 0.6;
--match_metric specifies the metric for deduplication of subgraph results. The default value is ios, which stands for intersection-over-sub-box (the area of ​​the intersection of two boxes divided by the area of ​​the smaller box). You can also select iou (the area of ​​the intersection of two boxes divided by the area of ​​their union). The accuracy varies depending on the dataset, but choosing ios will result in faster prediction speed.
